WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.170
Stay safe and make digital payments work for you.

2
00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:08.210
This is the video for module 4 of Digital Payments and POS Basics.

3
00:00:09.460 --> 00:00:17.460
You can now pay and get paid in every common way. This module protects what you have built, from tricks and from a stolen phone.

4
00:00:18.710 --> 00:00:26.030
Then it puts your payments to work: a budget from your statement, the right way to collect business money, and a 30-day plan.

5
00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:35.170
Almost every trick creates hurry or confusion, so you hand over your card, PIN, OTP or goods before you check.

6
00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:44.480
For example, Comfort's card does not come out of an ATM in Uyo. A young man tells her to type her PIN again while he holds the slot.

7
00:00:45.730 --> 00:00:54.160
She recognises the pattern. She steps back, does not re-enter her PIN, and calls the number saved in her phone to block the card.

8
00:00:55.410 --> 00:00:58.560
She lost a card, which can be replaced, not her savings.

9
00:00:59.810 --> 00:01:11.140
After a failed payment, fake customer care accounts reply on social media asking for your PIN, OTP or a reversal fee. Real banks never ask for these.

10
00:01:12.390 --> 00:01:19.370
Sellers are targeted too. A customer shows a transfer receipt when the queue is long. Check your own history first.

11
00:01:20.620 --> 00:01:29.040
A customer pays, collects, then tells his bank the payment failed. Your APPROVED receipt and record book entry will answer the dispute.

12
00:01:30.290 --> 00:01:38.810
And if someone says he is from your terminal provider and must take your terminal, call the provider's official number before handing anything over.

13
00:01:40.060 --> 00:01:54.180
For example, Folake's phone is snatched on a bus in Lagos at 6:15 pm. At 6:20 she borrows a colleague's phone and calls her bank on the number written on her card, to block mobile and USSD banking.

14
00:01:55.430 --> 00:01:59.870
At 6:30 she calls her wallet provider, from the number in her notebook.

15
00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:07.500
At 6:45 she calls her network to block the SIM, so no one can receive her OTPs.

16
00:02:08.750 --> 00:02:17.790
Next morning she finds no debits. Keep your support numbers on paper too. Lock your phone and apps, and hide OTP previews on the lock screen.

17
00:02:19.040 --> 00:02:31.860
Download last month's statement and sort the debits into five or six groups, like food, transport, airtime and data, bills, business stock and charges. Do not count moves between your own accounts.

18
00:02:33.110 --> 00:02:44.780
For example, Hadiza, a caterer in Abuja, found 16,000 naira went on small airtime and data top-ups. Any debit you do not recognise? Report it to your bank at once.

19
00:02:46.030 --> 00:02:53.820
So she will buy one monthly data plan instead. Pick one change, and read the terms before using any app savings feature.

20
00:02:55.070 --> 00:03:02.620
Use direct transfer for customers you know, POS for cards in person, and a payment link for new customers far away.

21
00:03:02.970 --> 00:03:18.070
Paystack's published local fee, checked in October 2026, is 1.5% plus 100 naira, with the 100 waived under 2,500. So Ifeoma's 2,000 naira order costs 30.

22
00:03:19.320 --> 00:03:22.990
A 15,000 naira order costs 325.

23
00:03:24.240 --> 00:03:35.570
A 200,000 naira order hits the cap, so the fee is 2,000. Prices change, so always check the official pricing page. And run the business through its own account.

24
00:03:36.820 --> 00:03:48.260
Plan 30 days with one focus a week. Week 1, setup and safety. Week 2, three payment types. Week 3, business or bills. Week 4, your statement review.

25
00:03:49.510 --> 00:04:02.630
Each week, Rahma spends ten minutes with her app history. Money in was 21,000, then 24,500, then 27,000, then 25,500 naira.

26
00:04:03.880 --> 00:04:14.730
98,000 in, against 68,000 out. Keep your receipts and tables for your certificate, and teach one other woman, by guiding her while she does it herself.

27
00:04:15.980 --> 00:04:33.670
To remember. Hurry is your signal to stop. No one genuine asks for your PIN, OTP or a fee to return your money. If your phone is stolen, block bank, wallet and SIM within the hour. Review your statement monthly, and match the payment method to the customer.

28
00:04:34.920 --> 00:04:43.130
Make your trick-spotting card, lock down your phone, write your emergency card, review last month's statement, and start your 30-day plan.

29
00:04:43.480 --> 00:04:45.420
Continue with the lessons below.
